== o5_kbd ==
nontrivial partitions of Omega: 14 (Bell(4) - 1 = 14)

-- A: the dichotomy on the classical carrier
A1  access (S4, passive z): 11 posteriors; all point masses reachable: True; extreme points = the 4 point masses: True; extreme points deterministic for all 15 partitions: True; balanced extreme point: False  -> True
A2  access (S4, passive z, KB-D z): 11 posteriors; all point masses reachable: True
A3  access (S4, KB-D z): 7 posteriors; no point mass: True; = uniform + 6 pair states: True; extreme points = the 6 pair states: True; x+ extreme and z-balanced: True; z-readout repeatable at x+ (posteriors (1/2, 1/2, 0, 0), (0, 0, 1/2, 1/2)): True; observe-and-forget(x+) = (1/4, 1/4, 1/4, 1/4) = uniform != x+: True  -> True
A4  access (S4, KB-D z, passive P) reaches every point mass, for each of the 14 nontrivial partitions P: 14/14  -> True
A5  pure-seed pattern (read z, correct, forget; swap; repeat; swap back): passive readout -> (1, 0, 0, 0) (point mass (0,0), probability 1); KB-D readout -> (1/2, 0, 1/2, 0) (pair state)  -> True
A6  passive decompositions on the A1 body for every partition at every reachable state: True; on the A3 body at x+: z-face = {z+}: True, 2x+ - z+ = (1/2, -1/2, 1, 0) not a state: True; separation control (segment [z+, z-]: passive, deterministic extreme points that are not point masses): True  -> True

-- B: candidate (a), incompleteness read as a memory bound
B1  1-bit memory, acceptance at the time (CNOT z->m, accept m=0, swap, CNOT z->m, accept m=0, swap): state (1, 0, 0, 0), acceptance probabilities 1/2, 1/2  -> point mass: True
B2  embedded, no acceptance: of 40320 bijections of (z, x, m), 18432 give a point-mass posterior -> True; |GL(3,2)| = 168, affine bijections 1344: posterior support sizes [2, 4], pair states occurring 6/6 -> knowledge-balanced posteriors: True
B3  frequencies given the preparation: coherent 1, dephased 1 (V = 0); memory-conditioned predictions: coherent 1, dephased [Fraction(1, 2)] (the record overwrote the preparation's record); with a fresh blank bit for the dephasing record: [Fraction(1, 1)]  -> True

-- C: candidate (b), the kernel recorder under a finite-memory bound
C1  recorder into a separate register: system marginal unchanged: True; recorder into the memory x: every outcome's posterior is the point mass (a, a): True  -> True
C2  576 bijections of (z, x, r) fixing z: perfect record into an unknown register: 0; into a blank register: 16, each keeping x as a known bijective relabeling: True  -> True

-- D: candidate (c), Lueders readout composed with a forgetful map
D1  KB-D z = forget_x o Lueders z on all 11 reachable states of A1 and A3, branch by branch: True
D2  the composite added to the stated access (passive readout kept): every point mass reachable (A2): True

-- E: candidate (d), symplectic couplings
E1  |GL(4,2)| = 20160; record couplings (z' = z, q' = z from q = 0), by class: symplectic & KB-D 32, symplectic & x kept 0, non-symplectic & KB-D 224, non-symplectic & x kept 128; with p known x' is a function of (z, x) in every case: True; the kickback coupling (x' = x + p) symplectic: True  -> True

normalization control: every reachable posterior of A1, A2, A3 is a probability vector: True

-- countercontrols (must be False)
CC1  CC-OK (False as required)
CC2  CC-OK (False as required)
CC3  CC-OK (False as required)
CC4  CC-OK (False as required)
CC5  CC-OK (False as required)

  A1: True
  A2: True
  A3: True
