VERDICT NO-GO-ON-STATED-ACCESS: with a passive repeatable readout in the access (the kernel's native Lueders
  readout on the classical carrier) the body is the simplex, every extreme state is deterministic, and KB-D's
  octahedron is excluded whatever is added (A1-A6); candidate (a) FAILED (procedures reach point masses with
  one memory bit; embedded, the memory bound restricts posteriors (B2aff = True) but not frequencies, V = 0);
  candidate (b) FAILED (the recorder is passive on the system or erases the memory to a known value);
  candidate (c) sources the KB-D instrument only, not its exclusivity; candidate (d) forces KB-D, CONDITIONAL
  on symplectic couplings together with an unknown pointer conjugate.
